hadiths[57]{hadithnumber,text}:
"47001","[470] Yahya told me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Abi Tamimah al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin: that Omar ibn Al-Khattab was among a people while they were reciting the Qur’an, so he went to fulfill his need, then he came back while they were reciting the Qur’an, and a man said to him O Commander of the Faithful, do you read the Qur’an without performing ablution? Then Omar said to him: Whoever told you this, I will take him to Islam. Muwatta Imam Malik Hadith: 470 Arabic Hadith:"
"47002","[470] Yahya told me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Abi Tamimah al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin: that Omar ibn Al-Khattab was among a people while they were reciting the Qur’an, so he went to fulfill his need, then he came back while they were reciting the Qur’an, and a man said to him O Commander of the Faithful, do you read the Qur’an without performing ablution? Then Omar said to him: Whoever told you this, I will take him to Islam. Muwatta Imam Malik Hadith: 470 Arabic Hadith:"
"47101","[471] Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Dawud ibn al-Husayn, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari, that Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said: Whoever misses his party during the night, and recites it when the sun goes down, until the noon prayer, has not missed it. Or as if he had overtaken you in front of Malik Hadith: 471 Arabic Hadith:"
"47102","[471] Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Dawud ibn al-Husayn, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari, that Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said: Whoever misses his party during the night, and recites it when the sun goes down, until the noon prayer, has not missed it. Or as if he had overtaken you in front of Malik Hadith: 471 Arabic Hadith:"
"47201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Dawud ibn al-Husayn from al- Araj from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari that Umar ibn al Khattab said"
"47202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Dawud ibn al-Husayn from al- Araj from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari that Umar ibn al Khattab said"
"47301","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said"
"47302","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah
ibn Umar said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant
him peace, said, 'Do not forbid the female slaves of Allah from (going
into) the mosques of Allah.' """
"47401","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr that Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari said that he had heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say"
"47402","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr that Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari said that he had heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say"
"47501","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"47502","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"47601","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from A'isha"
"47602","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from A'isha"
"477","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said that Abasa (Sura 80) was sent down about Abdullah ibn Umm Maktum. He came to the Prophet"
"478","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"479","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith at-Taymi from Abu Salama ibn Abd ar Rahman that Abu Said said that he had heard the Messenger of Allah"
"480","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that it took Abdullah ibn Umar eight years to learn Surat al-Baqara. (Sura)"
"481","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Yazid"
"482","And it was narrated to me from Malik, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, that he said: I saw Abdullah ibn Umar prostrating twice in Surah Al-Hajj."
"483","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abdullah ibn Dinar said"
"484","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from al-Araj that Umar ibn al Khattab recited Surat an-Najm (Sura 53) and prostrated in it"
"485","[485] Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abi Sa’sa’a, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Saeed Al-Khudri said that he heard a man reciting “Say: He is Allāh is One,” repeating it. So when the next morning, he went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he mentioned that to him, and it was as if a man was saying it, so the Messenger of God, peace and blessings be upon him, said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, it is equivalent to a third. The Qur’an."
"486","[486] And he told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ubaid bin Hunayn, the client of the family of Zayd bin Al-Khattab, that he said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: I came with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he heard a man reciting (Say: He God is One.) Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is obligatory, so I asked him what, O Messenger of God? He said: The jinn. Abu Hurairah said: So I wanted to go to him and give him good tidings, then I was afraid that I would miss lunch with him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I had lunch with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then I went to the man and found him gone, lying in front of Malik Hadith: 486 Arabic Hadith:"
"487","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ubaydullah ibn Abd ar-Rahman that Ubayd ibn Hunayn"
"488","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Humayd ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf had told him that Surat al-Ikhlas (Sura 112) was equal to a third of the Qur'an"
"489","And it was narrated to me from Malik, from Sumayy, the freed slave of Abu Bakr, from Abu Salih Al-Saman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever says, \Subhan Allah wa bihamdihi\"" (Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him) one hundred times in a day"," his sins will be erased"," even if they were like the foam of the sea."""
"490","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Abu Ubayd, the freed slave of Sulayman ibn Abd al-Malik, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laithi, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: \Whoever says 'Subhan Allah' thirty-three times"," and 'Allahu Akbar' thirty-three times"," and 'Al-hamdulillah' thirty-three times"," and completes the hundred by saying: 'La ilaha illa Allahu wahdahu la sharika lah"," lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu wa huwa ala kulli shay'in qadir","' his sins will be forgiven"," even if they were like the foam of the sea.\"""""
"491","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Umarah ibn Sayyad, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, that he heard him say concerning the enduring good deeds: \It is the saying of the servant: 'Allahu Akbar","' 'Subhan Allah","' 'Al-hamdulillah","' 'La ilaha illa Allah","' and 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah.'\"""""
"492","Yahya related to me from Malik that Umara ibn Sayyad had heard Said ibn al Musayyab say about abiding good deeds that they were a slave's saying 'Allah is greater' (Allahu akbar) and 'Glory be to Allah' (Subahana'llah) and 'Praise be to Allah' (al-hamdu lillah) and 'There is no god but Allah and there is no power and no strength except by Allah.' (La ilaha illa'llah wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa bi'llah)"
"493","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad said that Abu'd-Darda had said"
"494","Malik related to me from Nuaym ibn Abdullah ibn al-Mujmir from AIi ibn Yahya az-Zuraqi from his father that Rifaa ibn Rafi said"
"495","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"496","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"497","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"498","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abu Ubayd"
"499","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abu Abdullah al-Agharr and from Abu Salama from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"500","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith at-Taymi that A'isha"
"501","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad from Talha ibn Ubaydullah ibn Kariz that the Messenger of Allah"
"502","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'zZubayr al-Makki from Tawus al-Yamani from Abdullah ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah"
"503","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z Zubayr al-Makki from Tawus al-Yamani from Abdullah ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah"
"504","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Jabir ibn Atik said that Abdullah ibn Umar had come to them in Bani Muawiya"
"505","Yahya related to me from Malik that Zayd ibn Aslam used to say"
"506","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abdullah ibn Dinar said"
"507","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab used to say"
"508","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said"
"509","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"510","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"511","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"512","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abu'd-Darda used to rise in the middle of the night and say"
"513","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar from Abdullah as-Sunabihi that the Messenger of Allah"
"514","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said that the Messenger of Allah"
"515","Yahya related to me from Malik that al-Ala ibn Abd ar-Rahman said"
"516","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"517","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from al Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"518","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab used to say"
"519","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from as-Sa'ib ibn Yazid that he saw Umar ibn al-Khattab beating al-Munkadir for praying after asr"
